<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    The home-screen widget: what you are listening to, a transport, and what to carry on with.

    `minWidth`/`minHeight` are the smallest the launcher may make it — two cells by one, which is
    the size at which the episode and one button still fit. `minResizeHeight` is smaller than
    `minHeight` on purpose: it is the floor a *resize* may reach, and a user who drags the handle
    up should get the compact face rather than be refused. `targetCellWidth`/`targetCellHeight` are
    what a launcher on Android 12 and later actually places, and they are the size the shelf appears
    at, because that is the widget as it is meant to be seen.

    `updatePeriodMillis` is zero, and that is not an omission. The widget follows playback by
    collecting it — see NowPlayingWidget — so a periodic broadcast would wake the app to redraw a
    thing that has not changed. The platform's minimum is half an hour in any case, which is both
    far too slow to follow an episode and far too often to do nothing.

    `resizeMode` allows both axes: the two responsive sizes differ in height, and a user who wants
    it wider is asking for longer titles, which costs nothing.
-->
<appwidget-provider xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:description="@string/widget_description"
    android:minWidth="180dp"
    android:minHeight="100dp"
    android:minResizeWidth="180dp"
    android:minResizeHeight="100dp"
    android:targetCellWidth="4"
    android:targetCellHeight="3"
    android:previewImage="@drawable/ic_launcher_foreground"
    android:initialLayout="@layout/glance_default_loading_layout"
    android:resizeMode="horizontal|vertical"
    android:updatePeriodMillis="0"
    android:widgetCategory="home_screen" />
